                <pb facs="0394" n="302" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg302"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. von Holleben.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-02-28"><hi rendition="#italic">February 28,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Ambassador</hi>: I take pleasure in
                    acquainting you that the President, to whom I referred the memorandum you left
                    with me this morning, has instructed General Otis and Admiral Dewey to assume
                    the protection of German citizens and those hitherto enjoying German protection
                    in the Philippines.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
